    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a clever pivot, but I'm looking at the actual trial data again... the report doesn't actually say the competitor's side effects are \"persistent.\" It says they are similar, just less frequent. If a doctor calls us out on that, we're basically making things up to drive sales. Is there a way to frame this that stays closer to the data while still making sure the reps don't lose the momentum on the sale?",
